{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","max_tokens":1024,"stream":true,"system":"You are a code assistant for a small Dart repository. Use the tools to read files; do not guess file contents. Paths are relative to the repository root.","tools":[{"name":"read_file","description":"Read one text file of the repository at the pinned commit.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Repository-relative path, e.g. lib/a.dart"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"list_directory","description":"List the files under one directory of the repository.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Repository-relative directory, e.g. lib"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}}],"tool_choice":{"type":"auto"},"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","block_binding":{"prefix_mismatch_behavior":"error"}},"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How many seconds in total does the sync client wait across all of its retries? The policy is split across lib/a.dart, lib/b.dart and the file that lib/a.dart imports. First read lib/a.dart and lib/b.dart together (call read_file for both in the same step), then read the imported file, then work out the per-attempt delays carefully and give the total."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_78Yunb1GslHCcyjwFJDYEWMK","name":"read_file","input":{"path":"lib/a.dart"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_70Ssrz8a1Iw9XBDct4s6aVBB","name":"read_file","input":{"path":"lib/b.dart"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_78Yunb1GslHCcyjwFJDYEWMK","content":"import 'c.dart';\n\n/// Retry policy for the sync client.\nconst retryBase = 3; // seconds\n"},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_70Ssrz8a1Iw9XBDct4s6aVBB","content":"/// Number of retries after the first failure.\nconst retryCount = 5;\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_18B8JdoPi4kUYHMMLlaimWpY","name":"read_file","input":{"path":"lib/c.dart"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_18B8JdoPi4kUYHMMLlaimWpY","content":"/// Backoff shape used by lib/a.dart.\nconst multiplier = 2;\nconst maxDelay = 20; // seconds, cap applied to every attempt\n// delay(n) = min(retryBase * multiplier^n, maxDelay) for n = 0 .. retryCount - 1\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sync client waits **61 seconds** in total across its 5 retries.\n\nThe three files contribute as follows:\n- **lib/a.dart:** `retryBase = 3` seconds, and it imports `c.dart`.\n- **lib/b.dart:** `retryCount = 5` retries after the first failure.\n- **lib/c.dart:** `multiplier = 2` and `maxDelay = 20` seconds. Its comment gives the formula `delay(n) = min(retryBase * multiplier^n, maxDelay)` for n = 0 to retryCount − 1.\n\nPer-attempt delays:\n\n| Retry (n) | Uncapped (3 × 2ⁿ) | Delay after cap |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 3 | 3 |\n| 1 | 6 | 6 |\n| 2 | 12 | 12 |\n| 3 | 24 | 20 |\n| 4 | 48 | 20 |\n\nSum: 3 + 6 + 12 + 20 + 20 = **61 seconds**.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: lib/a.dart imports only `c.dart`, not `b.dart`. Nothing in `a.dart` references `retryCount`, so the link to `b.dart` exists only through the comment in `c.dart`. I used `retryCount = 5` from `b.dart` because that is the value the formula's comment refers to."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"If retryCount were changed to 8 and maxDelay to 30, what would the total wait be? Work it out from what you already read; do not call tools."}]}]}